_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The repaired network scores **45.4 veh-h on dev**, against 214.3 for the start network and 44.5 for the network with every detector working. All three files are in `work/`: `weights.npz`, `NOTES.md` and `predictions.json`.\n\n**What I changed and why:** with W2 reading empty, the network locked into EW_through for good. Both left-turn pockets backed up into the upstream lanes, and the network read those queues as through traffic. I changed only first-layer weights:\n- **Twin substitution:** the east left pocket (E2) now feeds the weights that used to read W2. It has the same geometry and demand and is served by the same phase.\n- **Time term:** a long green on any phase other than EW_left now pushes toward EW_left, and the term is never positive during EW_left itself. Without it, hidden W2 cars were stranded once E2 emptied: the first version left 2 and 5 vehicles at the drain cap.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 320 of 7428 (limit 371), all in W1.\n\n**Simulator calls:** 2 of 10.\n\n| version | low | nominal | high | mean | vehicles left at cap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| twin only | 34.8 | 45.6 | 57.5 | 46.0 | 2 and 5, in two episodes |\n| **final** | 34.9 | 45.1 | 56.1 | **45.4** | none |\n\n**Known risk:** a lone car on N1 (north straight) can still go unserved. This comes from the original network and happens even with working detectors. It's rare in the recorded data.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 35.1, nominal 45.4, high 56.6.","ttft_ms":2831,"type":"result","duration_ms":694985,"uuid":"a3688788-5ee9-4bed-a67f-466a3fb13431","ttft_stream_ms":2683,"time_to_request_ms":57,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":2,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":1,"message_prep":1,"model_conf